Based on my analysis, the endpoint uses `ProjectAlertRulePermission` (scope-based auth) plus a `can_edit_alert_rule` helper. The key authorization concern is the `target == "me"` branch: when `user_id` is set, the helper only checks org membership and skips the team-membership check that applies to org-wide snoozes. This lets a user snooze a rule they cannot otherwise edit.

